# /etc/systemd/system/wingmen-wake-backstop-sweep.service
# gzb-local wake BACKSTOP sweep (Nazim #43218; op#11297). The reliability FLOOR under the gzb
# realtime wingmen-agent-wake-subscriber (the #111 doorbell): a periodic reconciler that
# re-wakes any gzb recipient with a directed bus row rotting unread, independent of the
# realtime WS. The hub confirmed gzb runs ONLY the subscriber today (no sweep, no cron), so a
# missed doorbell to a gzb lane is NEVER retried — this closes that gap (#43158/#43163).
#
# Peer of the Mini instance (launchd dev.wingmen.wake-backstop-sweep). TWO instances are SAFE:
#  - wakes are HOST-LOCAL: the sweep's cross-host-liveness / dead-foreign logic (PR#139) only
#    pokes recipients this host can serve, so Mini and gzb never double-wake the same lane.
#  - the per-row delivery ceiling ($HOME/.wingmen_state/rownudge) is PER-HOST by design (a
#    local FS dir, not shared/DB), so each host counts only its OWN deliveries — correct,
#    since a gzb lane is only ever woken from gzb.
# Honors AUTO_WAKE_ENABLED (from the env below): observe-only (dry) when the kill-switch is
# off — same arming as the realtime subscriber.
#
# ARMED (Fable audit 2026-09-30 B-1 (iv), op#23531 PR A): the `--dry-run` observe-first
# stage (Nazim #43240 C3) is over. The two-instance safety it waited for is now in code:
# quiesce/stuck-page are HOST-GATED (a sweep only sets skipped_at / pages for a lane whose
# fresh agent_status heartbeat names ITS OWN host — the Mini can no longer quiesce gzb rows,
# and vice versa), the re-wake cap counts VERIFIED deliveries (not age), and transient
# doorbell outcomes leave pending markers this instance retries. gzb's lanes were the ones
# nobody retried (#46579 sat 14 min); this instance is the retry.
# STAGED, NOT ENABLED. The hub installs + enables + starts (Nazim-gated cutover):
#   sudo cp deploy/wingmen-wake-backstop-sweep.service /etc/systemd/system/
#   sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl enable --now wingmen-wake-backstop-sweep
#   systemctl status wingmen-wake-backstop-sweep   # confirm active + the "wake-backstop-sweep up ... dry_run=False" banner
# Reversible: `sudo systemctl disable --now wingmen-wake-backstop-sweep`.
#
# HOST-PATH CHECK (hub, confirm before enable — I can't see gzb's FS): this assumes the orch
# checkout is $HOME/wingmen/orchestrator for User=gazzai and the fetch-secrets .env is at
# /dev/shm/wingmen-secrets/.env (matching wingmen-irsyad-autoscaler.service). If either differs
# on gzb, adjust WorkingDirectory / the env path below. FAIL-LOUD (Nazim #43240 C2): a missing
# env file exits 1 BEFORE the banner (the daemon needs DATABASE_URL; a swallowed missing-env
# would otherwise print 'up' then loop 'no DATABASE_URL' forever); a wrong orch dir fails the cd.
[Unit]
Description=Wingmen wake BACKSTOP sweep (gzb-local reliability floor) — gzb
After=network-online.target wingmen-fetch-secrets.service
Wants=network-online.target
Requires=wingmen-fetch-secrets.service

[Service]
Type=simple
User=gazzai
WorkingDirectory=/home/gazzai/wingmen/orchestrator
# Shared tmpfs .env (fetch-secrets) — SAME env source as the hub's other units — gives
# DATABASE_URL (bus) + AUTO_WAKE_ENABLED. Login shell so the venv resolves for gazzai.
ExecStart=/bin/bash -lc 'cd "$HOME/wingmen/orchestrator" && { [ -r /dev/shm/wingmen-secrets/.env ] || { echo "backstop: secrets env missing at /dev/shm/wingmen-secrets/.env" >&2; exit 1; }; }; set -a; . /dev/shm/wingmen-secrets/.env; set +a; exec .venv/bin/python3 nervous_system/wake_backstop_sweep.py'
Restart=always
RestartSec=6

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
